## FOR RECORDS (NO text of yours in any project file: copy into STATUS FOR RECORDS as RELAYED)
- The OXPd 1.x client imports a CA certificate into a device's OXPd CA store and removes it (HP's `ImportCertificate` and `RemoveCertificate`, admin), each a dry run unless executed; it takes ONE DER certificate of 1 to 10240 bytes whose basic constraints name an authority; an import's undo is the remove of the same certificate. It reads the store (`ExportCertificates`, admin) through the writer only, answered only when every entry is one certificate; the read catalogue is unchanged.
- The lab's `oxpd1 write --write ImportCaCertificate|RemoveCaCertificate --certificate <file>` takes ONE CA certificate file (a file holding a private key refused before anything is read from it); an executed import reads the store first and writes nothing when the certificate is there; an answered import or remove reads the store after and says whether it is there; `undo-owed` owes the remove of an import.
- Named limits: not run against a device; whether the M577 takes the development root (owed item 103), how it exports an entry and whether it then uses the CA are UNMEASURED; a fault's subcode is not read; a certificate added between the read and the import is not seen.
- Nothing here has run against a device: the device run of first-run row 3 is a separate kit.

